{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve","id":1141524,"title":"Is it just me, or is the New Dawn pretty easy to achieve?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-18T13:49:43-07:00","id":1141524,"title":"Is it just me, or is the New Dawn pretty easy to achieve?","content":"So my group just got second edition, and I decided to make good use of it in our newest campaign. Within 4 game sessions I'd achieved the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> I read the book fairly quickly, since we got it right before the campaign started, but I think I had the rules right. I mastered all 3 roles in 8 different Refinements, nailed all the universal milestones (including making another Promethean out of a hunter that tried to take my group down) and boom, I was human. <br /> <br /> I'll admit, it was a bit of an unorthodox campaign setup. The other characters in my group were a Sin-Eater and a Beast, and we were meandering around Arcadia meeting all sorts of critters and having bizarre experiences which probably helped me hit some milestones that might be harder to complete in other circumstances.<br /> <br /> I'm not unhappy with the game. As with any rpg or boardgame it wasn't perfect, but there were a lot of fun things involved with it, and I had a blast. So, just to be clear, I'm not calling this out as a problem.<br /> <br /> I'm more curious...has anyone else had this kind of quick race to the endgame experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T15:11:03-07:00","id":1141555,"title":"","content":"This seems... incredibly uncommon, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Could you elaborate on the roles you did, how you achieved the Milestones, and how you learned those Paths? Since some are restricted access.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T15:21:21-07:00","id":1141558,"title":"","content":"While I haven't got the chance to actually play a Promethean game, having only read the 2e book, by the looks of it it seems you had a pretty lenient Storyteller. It's not a bad thing, since you said you had a good time, but it is indeed unorthodox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:11:23-07:00","id":1141572,"title":"","content":"That is... how long where game sessions? How many times did you elpis glimpse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T16:19:39-07:00","id":1141577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1141555#post1141555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This seems... incredibly uncommon, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Could you elaborate on the roles you did, how you achieved the Milestones, and how you learned those Paths? Since some are restricted access.</div> </div> </div> </div>How long did it take your group to reach the New Dawn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T17:09:40-07:00","id":1141591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1141577#post1141577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How long did it take your group to reach the New Dawn?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the games I played? None so far. Heck, 2 roles per session would have been a lot and uncommon, but just going by the maths, he did about 6 roles per session, which is immense! <br /> + hit all the roles and paths he had to without fail, which is different from my experience. Elpis is not alway clear, sometimes you stumble, sometimes you fail, have setbacks etc.<br /> But those moments are part of what makes the game so intriguing to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not saying they did it wrong, obviously they enjoyed it so hey, more power to them. Just very surprised and curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T17:17:14-07:00","id":1141594,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's bananas. It sounds like a fun campaign but that's not at all how it usually goes. What kind of stuff did you do to fulfill your Roles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T17:40:20-07:00","id":1141599,"title":"","content":"Was your character in a Role per scene? Holy hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T18:10:05-07:00","id":1141609,"title":"","content":"Maybe your st rushed you through, so you can become a mage ir draculer or changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T20:02:25-07:00","id":1141631,"title":"","content":"How the heck did you manage to complete six Roles per session? In my (admittedly limited) experience, it takes closer to six sessions per Role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T22:14:54-07:00","id":1141663,"title":"","content":"That does sound pretty exceptional. After 19 sessions my Promethean group has completed three roles across the three of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T22:17:01-07:00","id":1141664,"title":"","content":"I don't think I've felt a sense of wonder like this in a while. Please tell us the story of how this happened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 09-19-2017, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T23:30:38-07:00","id":1141673,"title":"","content":"I don't have the book or character on me because my group keeps our rpg stuff in the same spot so we don't have to keep lugging them around, so I'll do my best to clarify without much reference material to backup my memory.<br /> <br /> Let me start by saying that my game sessions last around 6 to 8 hours, so it's a decent amount of time.<br /> <br /> I got into the complex Refinements with Athanors. Exceptional successes let you make a Mentor and Furnace at the same time, and with a Beast on the team, and the Inspired condition, exceptional successes aren't hard to get.<br /> <br /> I did a lot of different Roles, and found most of them fairly easy to complete. I started out in Ferrum, and completed the Martyr Role by surviving my first serious fight (surviving stuff a human couldn't). I got the Exemplar Role by being acknowledged as a world class athlete (5 Dex, 5 Athletics, Parkour Merit) pretty easily. The other Role has a Milestone for beating a superior foe in single combat, and another for doing it with strategic positioning. That one was a bit harder, but not too bad. I don't remember a lot of the order I took through other Refinements, but quite a few were pretty simple. An Argentum Role has a Milestone that completes when you are prepared for a specific supernatural threat, and that same Refinement has a power that turns your aura into a specific bane for pretty much any critter you come across so that wasn't so bad. Savage has a Milestone for terrorizing a community, and I got into a fight with some hunters in a city. A couple of area effect lightning bolts and spending enough pyros to spark a firestorm covered that one. Phosphorum has the Daredevil Role which requires you to take self destructive non-fatal risks, I got that one by drinking a bunch of poisons on a bet with a Slasher. Obviously those are some of the easier examples, but a lot of them have a similar difficulty.<br /> <br /> Didn't do a lot of Elpis stuff. I was an Extempore and so didn't have access to Azothic memory. I did have an Azothic object, which one paragraph implies ties you to Azothic memory, but since that didn't lend itself to rules text it was largely ignored. I was in a group with some magical information gathering powers though, so that was pretty helpful. Although, since you can induce your own Elpis visions, and there's a Sensorium power to interpret all sybolism maybe it wasn't so different.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it really felt rushed. I was actually having a really hard time keeping track of all the new alembics being added to my character as the Roles flew by. My character sheet looks like one giant eraser burn. Fun though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:13:05-07:00","id":1141676,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5991_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5991\" data-vbnamecard=\"5991\">Akaru</a> You clearly had access to the milestones and metagamed your way into making them happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T00:19:51-07:00","id":1141678,"title":"","content":"Thanks for writing that up!<br /> <br /> I'm looking back at my book now, because I'm wondering if my reading of certain systems is right. It seemed obvious to me that the Mentor Athanor was only for passing on the Refinement you just finished to someone else, but it looks like the text doesn't actually say that except by implication on 94. I also figured that forcing an Elpis Vision was limited to once per story, full stop, but it doesn't actually state whether you cause a Wasteland when you try again <i>and </i>you can't roll again at all.<br /> <br /> I think the big difference is that you're expected to spend game time just inhabiting the Role and playing it out, and looking for an interesting Milestone opportunity when it arises. There are systems built around learning your character's custom/specific Milestones, you're not really expected to know them already. You don't need to be spending a whole story in one Role, but checking off one of the example Milestones as soon as possible feels like fast forwarding to the climax. Sure, you know how it ends, but the point was to sit down for a while and enjoy watching a movie.<br /> <br /> Having said that, different session length and pacing is a factor. It sounds like you rolled for New Dawn after playing for 30 hours or so. My IRL group plays for like 2-3 hours, so that would be ~12 sessions for us. I could see one or two PCs completing the Pilgrimage after 12 sessions if they were really going after it. I think 2 Roles every 3 chapters is a brisk but reasonable pace, and you can try the New Dawn after just 8 Roles.<br /> <br /> (aside: does anyone other than the players read Muddy Waters? Earth is definitely shooting to end her journey at 8 Roles if we get that far. Thinking about pace and the range of New Dawn outcomes makes me want to play a character who just wants out ASAP.)<br /> <br /> Now I'm wondering about the other PCs' endgame stuff. Did the Beast become Incarnate? Did the Sin-Eater found a Tier 3 Krewe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 09-19-2017, 03:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T07:06:05-07:00","id":1141733,"title":"","content":"Did I have access to Milestones and metagame them? ...kinda? I mean, the exact same part of the book that has the roles you embody has the milestones to complete them. I know these are just the most common, and there are more possibilities out there but it was a pretty good bet that some of them would be the ones from the book, and the others would be similar. So some of them I had no idea were coming, but others I had a pretty good idea about, simply by reading the parts of the book that I needed to play the game. So...kinda, yeah. <br /> <br /> I too got the impression that you're expected to take awhile inhabiting the role, and when I play as a Promethean in the future I'm planning on working with my storyteller beforehand to try to make that happen. Still, it seems like if you bumble into your Milestone early you'd want to move on. Especially since committing to a Role can cease disquiet but cause an automatic tainted wasteland anytime you act against the Role, which includes using your powers.<br /> <br /> Well, we're not really at the endgame as a whole, no. The beast isn't incarnate yet, although I'm sure that's what he's shooting for, and I have very little doubt he'll get there. The Sin-Eater's got a lot of the manifestations and keys, but his endgame is more about saving his granddaughter from a True Fae than any Geisty stuff, and we're all pitching in to help so while it's going to be very very difficult hopefully we'll manage it. We'd normally hit endgame around the same time, but we were all surprised when I hit New Dawn so quickly. As for my newly minted human, I continued to be useful with a large array of fighting styles, but my exposure to the supernatural pretty quickly drove me to integrity 0. And last session it ended with a cliffhanger that makes me think I'm about to get Vamped, so more endgame stuff is theoretically on the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T12:33:38-07:00","id":1141845,"title":"","content":"A couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> First, you don't automatically get to use the Milestones listed in the book. Those are examples of the sort of thing that <i>might</i> count as a Milestone. Whether or not it <i>does</i> count as a Milestone depends entirely on the Storyteller: he's supposed to come up with one Milestone for each Role you take on, and you have to figure out what that Milestone is. In fact, the game kinda sorta assumes that the samples Milestones found in the book generally <i>won't</i> work, because the Storyteller will have come up with another that's tailored to your particular Promethean's story. <br /> <br /> As for the loss of Integrity: which New Dawn option did you take? Because if you took the one where you remember the supernatural, your quick drop to Integrity 0, while technically according to the rules, violates their spirit. I'd recommend a house rule where the Redeemed who chose to retain their memories operate more along the lines of the Hunter 2e Code that was previewed recently: in particular, \u201cwitnessing the supernatural\u201d becomes \u201cwitnessing a particular supernatural phenomenon for the first time\u201d. That should greatly cut back on the number of Breaking Points you experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T13:11:19-07:00","id":1141863,"title":"","content":"A couple of responses:<br /> <br /> First, you're absolutely right. Because of the rushed beginning to the game, we more heavily relied on the examples than we normally would. Not all of the Milestones were directly from the book, but enough were that it certainly was a factor in the speed increase of the game. That being said, you only technically need 8 roles completed to achieve New Dawn, and while I'm not 100% sure that I got that many without the specific book examples, I probably did, and it would have been close at the very least.<br /> <br /> The loss of Integrity came mostly from supernatural phenomenon, yes, but actually, didn't really violate the spirit. My first choice was to forget, but then as soon as my I saw my Beast friend's Horror (I was in his Lair at the time) I hit my first breaking point. So I chose my one time only do-over, and remembered everything. My storyteller never made me roll for Supernatural occurrences that I'd already seen (whether it was because he forgot the actual rule, or he chose to house rule it right then right there, I'll probably never know) but either way I ran into a vampire (who was actually a Demon undercover), an alchemical creation, a couple new fae-ish things, and some hunters lobbing powers I'd never seen. And then I was crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:32:52-07:00","id":1141900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1141863#post1141863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of responses:<br /> <br /> First, you're absolutely right. Because of the rushed beginning to the game, we more heavily relied on the examples than we normally would. Not all of the Milestones were directly from the book, but enough were that it certainly was a factor in the speed increase of the game. That being said, you only technically need 8 roles completed to achieve New Dawn, and while I'm not 100% sure that I got that many without the specific book examples, I probably did, and it would have been close at the very least.<br /> <br /> The loss of Integrity came mostly from supernatural phenomenon, yes, but actually, didn't really violate the spirit. My first choice was to forget, but then as soon as my I saw my Beast friend's Horror (I was in his Lair at the time) I hit my first breaking point. So I chose my one time only do-over, and remembered everything. My storyteller never made me roll for Supernatural occurrences that I'd already seen (whether it was because he forgot the actual rule, or he chose to house rule it right then right there, I'll probably never know) but either way I ran into a vampire (who was actually a Demon undercover), an alchemical creation, a couple new fae-ish things, and some hunters lobbing powers I'd never seen. And then I was crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Next time, just take the Scarred merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:52:03-07:00","id":1141956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1141863#post1141863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of responses:<br /> <br /> First, you're absolutely right. Because of the rushed beginning to the game, we more heavily relied on the examples than we normally would. Not all of the Milestones were directly from the book, but enough were that it certainly was a factor in the speed increase of the game. That being said, you only technically need 8 roles completed to achieve New Dawn, and while I'm not 100% sure that I got that many without the specific book examples, I probably did, and it would have been close at the very least.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, regarding the roles: Your ST has to come up with which ones are integral to your road - and not necessarily tell you all of them. So you will fumble around a bit, thinking you are progressing, and in a way you are, but not really - kind of like growing up, I guess. So yeah, it would most certainly take far longer.<br /> But if this was in the spirit of your game, you had fun, then all is well. If I read everything correctly, this <i>increased </i>your interest in a more traditional Promethean game, if anything, so yeah, that's cool!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:44:16-07:00","id":1141981,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I mean, I didn't have direct access to all of them or anything, but it does seem like any real amount of player knowledge is a bigger push for Promethean than a lot of other games. And yes. Definitely more interested in the traditional game. And the game itself. It's good stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T23:14:01-07:00","id":1142044,"title":"","content":"It sounds like your Storyteller missed something core to the spirit of <i>Promethean</i>; the Pilgrimage is supposed to be exactly that, a long and winding journey that tests you again and again, not something that can be knocked out over the course of a few sessions. I'm glad you had fun, but this is radically off-base from the intended experience of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T07:53:56-07:00","id":1142151,"title":"","content":"For regular mortals, integrity can't actually hit zero. By RAW once you're at 1 you just stay there. <br /> <br /> Hunters can, according to the previews, but that seems to be a side-effect of the code.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:13:04-07:00","id":1142158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1142151#post1142151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For regular mortals, integrity can't actually hit zero. By RAW once you're at 1 you just stay there. <br /> <br /> Hunters can, according to the previews, but that seems to be a side-effect of the code.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, seriously?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:53:45-07:00","id":1142170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1142158#post1142158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div> True. Its in the core book rules. Mortals cap at Integrity 1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T08:58:37-07:00","id":1142174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1142170#post1142170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> True. Its in the core book rules. Mortals cap at Integrity 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. The indomitable human spirit, I guess","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:03:10-07:00","id":1142177,"title":"","content":"I couldn't actually find it mentioned in the core, but it is mentioned in Mage. The writers have confirmed that it's supposed to be a general rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T12:19:14-07:00","id":1142255,"title":"","content":"Well, its more of a function that dropping down to zero serves no purpose. Integrity is a bulwark against losing your shit when confronted by crazy supernatural stuff. There's always a chance that, when you see something supernatural, it doesn't bother you - random chance of being through too much, etc. Having a chance die just means that you'll always fail, and that's not as exciting as having a chance and continuing to investigate things you shouldn't. <br /> <br /> Of course, mortal games often serve as a jumping off point to become another game line (sometimes hunters, othertimes you Awaken or get Embraced, or go half-splat, or just a blood doll, etc). So completely breaking is also not quite useful either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:14:06-07:00","id":1143558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Akaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1141524-is-it-just-me-or-is-the-new-dawn-pretty-easy-to-achieve?p=1141673#post1141673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the book or character on me because my group keeps our rpg stuff in the same spot so we don't have to keep lugging them around, so I'll do my best to clarify without much reference material to backup my memory.<br /> <br /> Let me start by saying that my game sessions last around 6 to 8 hours, so it's a decent amount of time.<br /> <br /> I got into the complex Refinements with Athanors. Exceptional successes let you make a Mentor and Furnace at the same time, and with a Beast on the team, and the Inspired condition, exceptional successes aren't hard to get.<br /> <br /> I did a lot of different Roles, and found most of them fairly easy to complete. I started out in Ferrum, and completed the Martyr Role by surviving my first serious fight (surviving stuff a human couldn't). I got the Exemplar Role by being acknowledged as a world class athlete (5 Dex, 5 Athletics, Parkour Merit) pretty easily. The other Role has a Milestone for beating a superior foe in single combat, and another for doing it with strategic positioning. That one was a bit harder, but not too bad. I don't remember a lot of the order I took through other Refinements, but quite a few were pretty simple. An Argentum Role has a Milestone that completes when you are prepared for a specific supernatural threat, and that same Refinement has a power that turns your aura into a specific bane for pretty much any critter you come across so that wasn't so bad. Savage has a Milestone for terrorizing a community, and I got into a fight with some hunters in a city. A couple of area effect lightning bolts and spending enough pyros to spark a firestorm covered that one. Phosphorum has the Daredevil Role which requires you to take self destructive non-fatal risks, I got that one by drinking a bunch of poisons on a bet with a Slasher. Obviously those are some of the easier examples, but a lot of them have a similar difficulty.<br /> <br /> Didn't do a lot of Elpis stuff. I was an Extempore and so didn't have access to Azothic memory. I did have an Azothic object, which one paragraph implies ties you to Azothic memory, but since that didn't lend itself to rules text it was largely ignored. I was in a group with some magical information gathering powers though, so that was pretty helpful. Although, since you can induce your own Elpis visions, and there's a Sensorium power to interpret all sybolism maybe it wasn't so different.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it really felt rushed. I was actually having a really hard time keeping track of all the new alembics being added to my character as the Roles flew by. My character sheet looks like one giant eraser burn. Fun though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So...if I'm reading you right, it sounds like you read the book, learned (out of character) what the example milestones for Roles were, and then used that as a walkthrough in-game? Is that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}